  {
   "created": 1790817525,
   "description": "One-step image upscale/restore via SeedVR2 7B Sharp (int8_convrot, Apache-2.0, ICLR 2026). Verified at 2x (1024->2048) and 4x (1024->4096): both sharp, no grid/halo artifacts, genuinely enhanced fine detail (tested on food photography with fine scallion/noodle texture). steps=1, cfg=1 is the official template default -- SeedVR2 is a one-step flow-matching refine, not a traditional multi-step diffusion upscaler, so this is intentional rather than under-configured.",
   "id": "seedvr2-upscale",
   "object": "model",
   "owned_by": "vivid-fish",
   "vivid_fish_backend": "comfyui",
   "vivid_fish_intent": "image.edit",
   "vivid_fish_manifest_version": "0.1.0",
   "vivid_fish_workflow": true,
   "vivid_fish_workflow_id": "image.edit.seedvr2-upscale"
  },
  {
   "created": 1790965962,
   "description": "Mask-bound inpaint combining Qwen-Image 2.1 with LanPaint (scraed/LanPaint; no dedicated Qwen 2.1 inpaint checkpoint exists, LanPaint is the community-consensus universal inpainting tool, updated for Qwen 2.1 support Sep 2026). Mask is the source image's own alpha channel (OpenAI edit-API convention: transparent = regenerate). KNOWN LIMITATION, reproduced in our own test and consistent with community reports (research-image.md): a faint horizontal blend seam/haze band can appear at the mask boundary on hard-edged masks. Mask feathering (mask_feather, default 48px) reduces but does not eliminate it -- this is flagged in the community as unresolved (\"neither fix is perfect\") as of Sep 2026. Prefer masks with generous feather/soft edges over pixel-exact cutouts.",
   "id": "qwen-image-2.1-inpaint",
   "object": "model",
   "owned_by": "vivid-fish",
   "vivid_fish_backend": "comfyui",
   "vivid_fish_intent": "image.edit",
   "vivid_fish_manifest_version": "0.1.0",
   "vivid_fish_workflow": true,
   "vivid_fish_workflow_id": "image.edit.qwen-image-2.1-inpaint"
  },
  {
   "created": 1790965962,
   "description": "2-image reference composite/edit via Qwen-Image 2.1's native multi-image conditioning (TextEncodeQwenImage21's Autogrow `images` input, tested up to 16 slots upstream; this workflow wires exactly 2 as required inputs). Verified: convincingly composites a subject from one reference onto the scene/lighting of another in a single pass, no separate masking/compositing step needed. Reference prompts should tag each image explicitly, e.g. \"<image1> shows X. <image2> shows Y. Combine them by...\". A 3-reference variant is not shipped: the gateway's static node-binding model (gateway/manifests.py _apply_mapping, flat node/input writes) cannot make an Autogrow sub-key conditionally present per request, so a 3rd \"optional\" slot would always inject a placeholder image as a real (if low-signal) reference. A 3-image variant needs gateway support for per-request Autogrow key pruning; this manifest keeps the tested 2-image shape.",
   "id": "qwen-image-2.1-edit-multiref",
   "object": "model",
   "owned_by": "vivid-fish",
   "vivid_fish_backend": "comfyui",
   "vivid_fish_intent": "image.edit",
   "vivid_fish_manifest_version": "0.1.0",
   "vivid_fish_workflow": true,
   "vivid_fish_workflow_id": "image.edit.qwen-image-2.1-edit-multiref"
  },
  {
   "created": 1790965962,
   "description": "Single-image instruction edit via Qwen-Image 2.1 (int8_convrot) + qwen3vl_8b_w4a8 text encoder + madebyollin texture-fix VAE. Community consensus (Sep 2026, r/StableDiffusion) ranks this the best local editor available, ahead of Flux.2 Klein 9B, especially for edits needing world knowledge. Output resolution tracks the input image. License: Qwen research license (disputed scope on Reddit re: output rights) -- flagged for legal review before commercial-use reliance per research-image.md.",
   "id": "qwen-image-2.1-edit",
   "object": "model",
